well saturday will mark 20 years since 9  11. and this week the i-team is bringing  you stories a southern nevada remembers  that fateful day vanessa murphy is here  with the story of one las vegas local  who was on the front lines vanessa  denise frank pizarro dealt with the  grief of losing fellow firefighters on 9  11. he also was part of the recovery  effort to find their bodies the pain and  trauma he lives with every day  i remember myself telling the chief  you know a lot of guys going to die  today  frank pizarro remembers the ride from  his new york city firehouse to the world  trade center on september 11 2001 where  destruction continued because there was  a verizon building that was a block over  and we had gone into search after the  first two towers have come down  and five minutes after we got out of  that that thing came down in the days  and months that followed we went digging  through the pile  hoping to find anything or anybody he  was part of search efforts it was  powerful because  we would find say a fireman from a  specific house  and all work would stop and we would  call that firehouse  so they could come and bring him out of  the hole and so it was it was a sight to  be seen the aisle would line up and  everybody would stand attention and  salute as he would be carried out  and this happened over and over and over  again 20 years later he remains proud to  wear the uniform i would do it all over  again you know it's it's probably the  best job in the world  and  i lost a lot of friends  and brothers and  that i'll never forget he retired in  2017 and then moved to las vegas like  many first responders at ground zero he  says he has health issues including lung  disease but that doesn't keep him from  his passion i decided that i'm going to  sing until i can't sing anymore  it's not as easy as it used to be  but i give everything i got  and i'm going to sing until the last  note comes out  from 9 11 tributes in southern nevada to  the world series in new york pizarro  continues to share his voice  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  and pizarro is going to sing at a  fundraiser on 9 11 here in las vegas he  also started a charity to help remember  fallen firefighters we have information  on both at 8newsnow.com
 

